From dca0ed16e564ab048405888952fd86f56ef9335a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chi Lang <chilang@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:06:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [V1][Pooling] Incremental pooling sessions: streaming input
 and in-place extend

A pooling request can take streaming input: each update carries new tokens
(with per-input readout offsets in PoolingParams.extra_kwargs["arc_gather"])
and resumes the paused session with the update's params. On the V2 GPU model
runner a resumed text-only request is extended in place, writing only the new
token ids, M-RoPE positions and block ids; stock re-adds the whole request
(O(session length)) on every append. An update that brings an image takes the
existing full re-add.

Modified by Atlas Futures, Inc., 2026 (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)).
Files: vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py, vllm/v1/engine/async_llm.py,
vllm/v1/request.py, vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py.

Upstream: not yet offered (planned RFC: incremental pooling sessions).

Signed-off-by: Chi Lang <chilang@gmail.com>
